                    {
                        "translation_id": "1535c7bb-d4d3-4c06-a61e-fdfc7b87287d",
                        "source_entry_id": "e40410fb-cf71-32cc-8c33-e16bfb22dec6",
                        "source_sense_id": "56ec5f68-9d16-3c9c-a49c-b25233aac94d",
                        "target_lang_word": "extension",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "extension",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bcf4503d-3e9e-3b65-83a2-0e31efd0eeeb",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4de6b5-efb8-3847-bc0a-c394f80fbe4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of extending; a stretching out; enlargement in length, breadth, or time; an increase."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7351c6a-7889-4403-8e63-8cfbcca6daf9",
                                                "sense_id": "bcf4503d-3e9e-3b65-83a2-0e31efd0eeeb",
                                                "text": "Next month the house is undergoing an extension."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b397fe8-16f4-43e3-96d1-2139c5169e68",
                                                "sense_id": "bcf4503d-3e9e-3b65-83a2-0e31efd0eeeb",
                                                "text": "Due to the unforeseen circumstances, you are allowed an extension of two weeks to complete the task."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12fce4c9-7838-495a-b7bd-53e850f4c142",
                                                "sense_id": "bcf4503d-3e9e-3b65-83a2-0e31efd0eeeb",
                                                "text": "\"Keep off Conductor Rails\" said red-painted notices at the platform ends, for third-rails were laid in many places even where electric trains never normally ran, and there had been many rumours of impending electrification of the Wirral, as a natural extension of the Mersey system, a quarter of a century before the change was actually made."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "83a3adb7-fd0d-3c22-a012-a51857b34875",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4de6b5-efb8-3847-bc0a-c394f80fbe4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being extended."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8a0e9ed-a2c6-45ba-93d1-7d0219826c30",
                                                "sense_id": "83a3adb7-fd0d-3c22-a012-a51857b34875",
                                                "text": "For station is properly no rest, but one kind of motion, relating unto that which physicians (from Galen) do name extensive or tonical; that is, an extension of the muscles and organs of motion, maintaining the body at length, or in its proper figure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a9b2411d-32a7-341d-800c-ca0cd645fa07",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4de6b5-efb8-3847-bc0a-c394f80fbe4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That property of a body by which it occupies a portion of space (or time, e.g. \\\"spatiotemporal extension\\\")."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "895f0b28-de49-3134-bdcd-35e9eed9da0c",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4de6b5-efb8-3847-bc0a-c394f80fbe4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A short exact sequence 1→H→E→G→1, or the group E therein."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3561fd01-fa4c-36f9-9326-579c77819243",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4de6b5-efb8-3847-bc0a-c394f80fbe4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A short exact sequence 0→B→E→A→0, or the object E therein."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dec4ddbe-9d8d-3636-a1ee-6e54b3806035",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4de6b5-efb8-3847-bc0a-c394f80fbe4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A part of a building that has been added onto the original."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b530f0ab-5cd9-3815-9cc8-2fdcbf0807f7",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4de6b5-efb8-3847-bc0a-c394f80fbe4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An outgrowth; a part of something that extends its capabilities."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92036e41-f58b-4fe1-a465-4ad5de72ec6a",
                                                "sense_id": "b530f0ab-5cd9-3815-9cc8-2fdcbf0807f7",
                                                "text": "Parents who treat their children as an extension of themselves"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab403435-c99a-4bce-bc49-bcd2ba44c63e",
                                                "sense_id": "b530f0ab-5cd9-3815-9cc8-2fdcbf0807f7",
                                                "text": "My research is an extension of the work of my mentor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c693a712-e122-442f-b18a-ebf15fe9eaf3",
                                                "sense_id": "b530f0ab-5cd9-3815-9cc8-2fdcbf0807f7",
                                                "text": "In smaller communities, the public schools are virtual extensions of each town's chief religion — \"educating\" kids to all the prejudices of that belief."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac17da06-bba0-3081-932e-a9b68965622e",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4de6b5-efb8-3847-bc0a-c394f80fbe4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Capacity of a concept or general term to include a greater or smaller number of objects; — correlative of intension."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8706ca3-4987-470d-9be8-1ba9415cabec",
                                                "sense_id": "ac17da06-bba0-3081-932e-a9b68965622e",
                                                "text": "Perversely, we love John Wick himself. That lethal, bereaved assassin is a good bad guy for our times, the natural extension of Tony Soprano, Walter White and all the other heroic antiheroes the culture has embraced."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "679f025b-a9eb-41aa-a6c3-72b93d582745",
                                                "sense_id": "ac17da06-bba0-3081-932e-a9b68965622e",
                                                "text": "In addition to concepts and conceptual senses, Frege holds that there are extensions of concepts. Frege calls an extension of a concept a ‘course of values’. A course of values is determined by the value that the concept has for each of its arguments. Thus, the course of values for the concept __ is a dog records that its value for the argument Zermela is the True and for Socrates is the False, and so on. If two concepts have the same values for every argument, then their courses of values are the same. Thus, courses of values are extensional."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3320d4bc-b4f9-3bbb-82de-a61343c9a95d",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4de6b5-efb8-3847-bc0a-c394f80fbe4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "semantic widening, broadening of meaning"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e851307d-8b3a-35cf-9f72-1b908664b58f",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4de6b5-efb8-3847-bc0a-c394f80fbe4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A written engagement on the part of a creditor, allowing a debtor further time to pay a debt."
                                        ],
